From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@tuta.io>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:03:00 +0800
Subject: power: supply: isolate the Piano USB connector on overtemperature

Monitor both factory connector thermistors and apply the board
temperature and rise-rate trips. Stop both charging paths and USB
source power, then drive the isolation MOS. Use UCSI presence and ADSP
attachment to require unplugging before a thermal trip can clear.

Keep the monitor running with an attached cable. Isolate a detached
connector for suspend and require fresh readings on resume. A
connection during restore or an uncertain GPIO write keeps charging
paused until isolation and recovery can be checked again.

Assert the connector MOS before ADSP transactions can delay isolation.

Keep the connector isolated when fresh VBUS contradicts a UCSI detach report. The original PD proxy exposes CID and USB online as separate values.

Signed-off-by: slwyts <slwyts@tuta.io>
